@groud @fire  thanks for looking at the PR and the review. I see a problem with this:

Let's say the user is dragging and dropping and they _release_ the mouse button on top of the section label. In this case, `MOUSE_EXIT` has not fired yet, but `DRAG_END` (which is not implemented in the case of this suggestion) has. As a result, even if the drag is finished the unfold will still occur, even if they move their mouse outside of the InspectorSection area. This could be partially solved by just doing:

```gdscript
	if (p_what == NOTIFICATION_MOUSE_EXIT) {
		dropping_unfold_timer->stop();
	}
```

But the problem would still occur if they finish the drag and leave their mouse inside the section area. 

This is... a really rare case, especially considering all this happens in 0.6 seconds, but it's still a slight inconsistency in behaviour. That's my thoughts - happy to change it if you guys think it's worth it.
